          dealing: '1. Dealer deals 3 cards to each player face down. 2. 4 cards are dealt face up to the table. 3. Dealing is counter-clockwise.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first to reach 21 points through captures and hand declarations.',
          gameplay: '1. Dealer gives 3 cards to each player, 4 face-up on table. 2. Declaration phase: players may announce Chorizo, Flor, Báciga, or Escalera before play. 3. In turn, each player plays one card to capture table cards that sum to 15, or adds a card to the table. 4. Escoba: capturing all table cards scores bonus. 5. When hands empty, dealer deals 3 more cards; repeat until deck exhausted. 6. Score: Oros (coins), Cartas (cards), Setenta (sevens). First to 21 wins.',
          keyRules: [
            '21 points wins the game.',
            'The 7 of Coins is the most valuable individual card.',
            'If the initial 4 cards on the table sum to 15 or 30, the Dealer takes them as 1 or 2 Escobas immediately.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Prioritize the 7 of Coins. Try to avoid leaving the table with a sum that allows an easy '15' for the next player.",
          intermediate: "Table Management: If you can't take a trick, play a card that makes the table total difficult to combine into 15 (e.g., if the table has a 4, don't play an Ace if you know the opponent has a 10/Sota).",
          advanced: "Communication (Partnerships): Use your lead to signal the suit of your 'Flor' or 'Escalera' to your partner without explicitly saying it.",
          tips: [
            "Winning the 'Setenta' (best sevens) is often the tie-breaker in close games.",
            "If you are close to 21, focus on 'Escobas'���they are the fastest way to move the dial.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
