          deckDescription: 'Traditional 40-card Spanish deck used for Escoba and Báciga, with four suits (Coins, Cups, Clubs and Swords). Each suit has Ace through 7 plus Sota, Caballo and Rey, and no jokers are included in the pack.',
          suitDescription: 'Four Spanish suits: Coins (oros), Cups (copas), Clubs (bastos) and Swords (espadas). Suits matter mainly for Setenta and for special scoring cards such as the seven of coins and the two of clubs in this Uruguayan Escoba family game.',
          rankDescription: 'Ten ranks per suit: Ace, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, Sota (jack), Caballo (horse) and Rey (king). For captures 1–7 count at face value, the Sota counts as 8, the Caballo as 9 and the Rey as 10 following the Escoba tradition.',
          dealPattern: '3 to player, 4 to table.',
          bettingLimits: 'NA',
          actions: {},
          handRankingSystem: 'Standard poker hand rankings.',
          rankingSystem: 'Capture + Declaration Bonuses',
          useTrump: false,
